<title>NETHERLANDS: Akzo sells Brazilian interests to DuPont.</title>
<headline>Akzo sells Brazilian interests to DuPont.</headline>
<dateline>ARNHEM, Netherlands 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch chemicals group Akzo Nobel NV said on Friday it had agreed to sell its Brazilian nylon activities to U.S. Dupont Co.</p>
<p>No financial details were disclosed.  </p>
<p>Akzo Nobel's interests are grouped in its Cobafi subsidiary, which also produces polyester fibres at a plant in Bahia. Akzo said Cobafi would continue to produce polyester after DuPont's acquisition of the nylon activities.</p>
<p>&quot;DuPont and Cobafi intend to cooperate at this production location in order to take advantage of available resources, such as personnel, services, untilities and supplies,&quot; Akzo said in a brief statement.</p>
<p>Akzo employs around 70,000 people in over 50 countries.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
